==Results==
Heinz Fischer beat Barbara Rosenkranz by scoring 79.3% of the vote.<ref name="bmi">{{cite web|url= http://www.bmi.gv.at/cms/BMI_wahlen/bundespraes/bpw_2010/Ergebnis.aspx|title= Bundespräsidentenwahl 2010|language= de|publisher= [[Federal Ministry of the Interior (Austria)|Federal Ministry of the Interior]]|access-date= 30 April 2010| archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20100429090253/http://www.bmi.gv.at/cms/BMI_wahlen/bundespraes/bpw_2010/Ergebnis.aspx| archive-date= 29 April 2010 | url-status= live}}</ref> Rosenkranz received 15.2%.<ref name="bmi"/> Rudolf Gehring came third by scoring 5.4%.<ref name="bmi"/>

Opinion polls had placed Fischer in a good position on the day of the election.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://news.xinhuanet.com/english2010/world/2010-04/25/c_13266842.htm|title=Austria holds presidential election|date=25 April 2010|access-date=25 April 2010|publisher=[[Xinhua News Agency]]|archive-date=10 June 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110610002708/http://news.xinhuanet.com/english2010/world/2010-04/25/c_13266842.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Fischer thanked the nation on television: "I am extremely happy and thank the Austrian population for having so much confidence in me".<ref name="CBC World">{{cite web|url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/austrian-president-cruises-to-2nd-term-1.898337|title=Austrian president cruises to 2nd term|date=25 April 2010|access-date=25 April 2010|publisher=[[CBC News]]|archive-date=26 January 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160126015954/http://www.cbc.ca/news/world/austrian-president-cruises-to-2nd-term-1.898337|url-status=live}}</ref>

Poor voter turnout – only 53.6% voted<ref name="bmi"/> – led again to calls by leaders for the post to be abolished.<ref>{{cite news|author=Scally, Derek|url=http://www.irishtimes.com/newspaper/world/2010/0426/1224269091601.html|title=Poor turnout gives Fischer hollow re-election victory|date=26 April 2010|access-date=26 April 2010|newspaper=[[The Irish Times]]|archive-date=17 November 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101117132505/http://www.irishtimes.com/newspaper/world/2010/0426/1224269091601.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

